# Coverage exceptions — a ratchet, not an amnesty.
#
# Format: <package> <minimum-percent> <wave that removes this entry> <why>
#
# Rules enforced by scripts/coverage-gate.sh:
#   - A listed package must stay at or above its recorded minimum. It can never
#     regress; lowering a number here is a rejected change, not a fix.
#   - When a listed package reaches the global 80% bar, the gate FAILS until its
#     entry is deleted. Exceptions cannot outlive their justification.
#   - An entry naming a package with no recorded coverage is STALE and fails.
#   - Anything not listed must reach 80%. New packages get no exception.

#
# Every entry below exists because the package is scheduled for replacement in a
# named wave. Writing tests today for code that W1–W6 deletes is waste; the
# ratchet stops it rotting in the meantime.

